irths","kind":"unsd","asOf":"2026-10-05","figure":{"value":271983,"what":"births registered (registration reported as virtually complete)","date":"2021","provisional":false,"estimated":false},"notes":["The Government of Ukraine has informed the United Nations that it is not in a position to provide statistical data concerning the Autonomous Republic of Crimea and the city of Sevastopol."],"unFigure":{"value":309089,"what":"UN figure for 2021","date":"2021","forecast":false},"gapPct":13.6,"verdict":"context","coverageDiffers":true,"links":[{"label":"UN Statistics Division: births and deaths (table 3)","href":"https://unstats.un.org/unsd/demographic-social/products/vitstats/seratab3.pdf"}]},{"key":"deaths","kind":"unsd","asOf":"2026-10-05","figure":{"value":714263,"what":"deaths registered (registration reported as virtually complete)","date":"2021","provisional":false,"estimated":false},"notes":["The Government of Ukraine has informed the United Nations that it is not in a position to provide statistical data concerning the Autonomous Republic of Crimea and the city of Sevastopol."],"unFigure":{"value":759006,"what":"UN figure for 2021","date":"2021","forecast":false},"gapPct":6.3,"verdict":"context","coverageDiffers":true,"links":[{"label":"UN Statistics Division: births and deaths (table 3)","href":"https://unstats.un.org/unsd/demographic-social/products/vitstats/seratab3.pdf"}]},{"key":"today","kind":"researched","text":"The UN's forecast assumed two thirds of Ukraine's refugees would be home by 2026. Newer counts don't show that: 4.36 million Ukrainians were under temporary protection in the EU in August 2026, more than in December 2024 (4.19 million), and the UN refugee agency recorded about 350,000 refugee returns in 2024–2025.","figure":{"value":4363955,"what":"Ukrainians under temporary protection in the EU","date":"2026-08-31"},"unFigure":null,"gapPct":null,"verdict":"context","links":[{"label":"UN assumption (table II.3.B, p. 49)","href":"https://population.un.org/wpp/assets/Files/WPP2024_Methodology-Report_Final.pdf"},{"label":"Eurostat: temporary protection","href":"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/view/migr_asytpsm/default/table?lang=en"},{"label":"UNHCR: refugees from Ukraine","href":"https://data.unhcr.org/en/documents/details/121051"},{"label":"UNHCR: returns","href":"https://api.unhcr.org/population/v1/population/?year=2025&coo=UKR"}],"quotes":[{"text":"Recent statistical analysis for 35 countries with ongoing refugee crises by […] (2024) also validates the projection assumption that two thirds of refugees will return to their country of origin within 5 years.","href":"https://population.un.org/wpp/assets/Files/WPP2024_Methodology-Report_Final.pdf"}],"accessed":"2026-10-29"},{"key":"net","kind":"researched","text":"The light bars for 2024 and 2025 are the UN's assumed return of two thirds of refugees (+2.85 million). Newer counts don't show it: Ukrainians under temporary protection in the EU rose to 4.36 million by August 2026, and the UN refugee agency recorded about 350,000 refugee returns in 2024–2025.","figure":{"value":348315,"what":"refugee returns to Ukraine recorded by UNHCR, 2024 and 2025 combined","date":"2025"},"unFigure":{"value":2850000,"what":"UN net migration assumed for 2024 and 2025 combined","date":"2025"},"gapPct":718.2,"verdict":"un-higher","links":[{"label":"UN assumption (table II.3.B, p. 49)","href":"https://population.un.org/wpp/assets/Files/WPP2024_Methodology-Report_Final.pdf"},{"label":"Eurostat: temporary protection","href":"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/view/migr_asytpsm/default/table?lang=en"},{"label":"UNHCR: returns","href":"https://api.unhcr.org/population/v1/population/?year=2025&coo=UKR"}],"quotes":[],"accessed":"2026-10-29"},{"key":"immigrants","kind":"researched","text":"The UN didn't newly assess Ukraine for 2024: it carried forward its 2020 estimate. Ukraine's last census was in 2001, and the mix of birth countries matches it, scaled down.","figure":null,"unFigure":null,"gapPct":null,"verdict":"context","links":[{"label":"UN key facts, p. 1","href":"https://www.un.org/development/desa/pd/sites/www.un.org.development.desa.pd/files/undesa_pd_2025_intlmigstock_2024_key_facts_and_figures_advance-unedited.pdf"}],"quotes":[{"text":"In the new edition of these data, a total of 60 countries and areas received a full reassessment of trends in the number of international migrants residing in the territory. For the remaining countries and areas, the estimates generated in 2024 reflect extrapolations of estimates published in the 2020 edition of the dataset.","href":"https://www.un.org/development/desa/pd/sites/www.un.org.development.desa.pd/files/undesa_pd_2025_intlmigstock_2024_key_facts_and_figures_advance-unedited.pdf"}],"accessed":"2026-10-29"}],"links":{"self":"https://fertility-tracker-live.vercel.app/api/v1/countries/UKR.json","countries":"https://fertility-tracker-live.vercel.app/api/v1/countries.json","risk":"https://fertility-tracker-live.vercel.app/api/v1/risk.json","docs":"https://fertility-tracker-live.vercel.app/api/","site":"https://fertility-tracker-live.vercel.app/country/UKR"}}
